From: Mixtile <support@mixtile.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: power_delivery: fusb302: keep the transceiver powered on handoff

U-Boot hands the port to the OS with the PD contract still live.  Powering the
transceiver down at that point leaves the chip unable to transmit, so it cannot
answer the GoodCRC for any message the source sends after U-Boot stops polling.
A source that does send one reads the silence as a dead link and drops VBUS to
vSafe0V, which resets a board running from that port.

PWR_MEDIUM clears the TX bit and PWR_HIGH clears the oscillator the BMC PHY
needs, so neither is usable here.  Skip the transition while a contract is up.

--- a/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c
+++ b/drivers/power/power_delivery/fusb302.c
@@ -965,12 +965,19 @@
 	int ret = 0;
 	unsigned int reg;
 
+	/*
+	 * Keep the transceiver powered while a contract is live.  PWR_MEDIUM
+	 * clears the TX bit, so the chip cannot answer the GoodCRC for anything
+	 * the source sends after U-Boot stops polling, and a source that does
+	 * send something treats the silence as a dead link and drops VBUS.
+	 */
+	if (attached && pd_capable)
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = fusb302_mask_interrupt(chip);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	if (attached && pd_capable)
-		reg = FUSB_REG_POWER_PWR_MEDIUM;
-	else if (attached)
+	if (attached)
 		reg = FUSB_REG_POWER_PWR_LOW;
 	else
 		reg = 0;
